<DocsLayout
  title="Audio"
  description="Load audio files, use the player, and work with live input."
>
  <h2>Loading an audio file</h2>
  <p>
    Click <strong>Load audio</strong> in the sidebar and pick a file.
    Supported formats include MP3, WAV, OGG, and other browser-supported
    audio types. The file is analyzed and its waveform appears in the
    player at the bottom of the window.
  </p>

  <h2>The player</h2>
  <div class="placeholder">Screenshot: The audio player</div>
  <p>The player provides:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Play / pause</strong> &mdash; starts or stops the audio and animation.</li>
    <li><strong>Progress bar</strong> &mdash; scrub to any point in the track.</li>
    <li><strong>Waveform</strong> &mdash; visual overview of the whole track.</li>
    <li><strong>Time display</strong> &mdash; current time and total duration.</li>
    <li><strong>Volume</strong> &mdash; playback volume (doesn't affect exported video).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Live input mode</h2>
  <p>
    Instead of a file, Astrofox can drive visuals from live input. Toggle
    <strong>Live mode</strong> in the player to switch the source.
  </p>
  <div class="placeholder">Screenshot: Live mode panel with source picker</div>
  <h3>Microphone</h3>
  <p>
    Select a microphone device from the list. Astrofox requests mic permissions
    from the browser. An oscilloscope replaces the waveform so you can see the
    live signal.
  </p>
  <h3>MIDI</h3>
  <p>
    Astrofox can also listen to a MIDI controller. Select a MIDI input device
    and Astrofox will route incoming note/CC data into the reactor system.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
